### Limitations the authors admit
- 2016ApJ...830L..37I: COM distribution is not resolved; acetone detection tentative; angular resolution insufficient to see distribution trends
- 2018A&A...616A..90C: Errors depend on LTE, optically thin and Gaussian assumptions; HC3N only 3 lines, two blended
- 2020MNRAS.496..394R: Single excitation temperature is a large source of uncertainty.
- 2020MNRAS.496..394R: Spectral index poorly constrained because bands 6 and 7 are adjacent; fluxes and globule mass are lower bounds.
- 2019NatAs...3..314L: XCLASS fit is imperfect; CH3OH lines likely optically thick, requiring 2-D modelling postponed
- 2025ApJS..276...49J: Fixed beam-filling factor makes column densities likely lower limits (factor ~2-3)
- 2025ApJS..276...49J: ~20% of lines unidentified
- 2018A&A...615A..28D: Dust masses and dust-to-gas ratios uncertain by about a factor of 5
- 2018A&A...615A..28D: Extended emission may be resolved out
- 2016ApJ...833...69D: rho(H2) is a lower limit as faint end not recovered; Poisson errors and cosmic variance large
- 2025A&A...694A.166C: 3 mm data cannot resolve the emission distribution in distant sources
- 2024ESC.....8..665M: Coarse resolution; morphology cannot be determined
- 2020MNRAS.492.1180R: Resolution too low to resolve cavity wall layers; speculative conclusions
- 2013ApJ...767...88W: Eight ambiguous redshifts hamper determination of the distribution shape; small sample
- 2013ApJ...767...88W: Dust temperatures not physical; lensing size-evolution bias cannot be excluded
- 2020A&A...644A.119P: Column densities may be underestimated by a factor of a few if lines are mildly optically thick
- 2020A&A...644A.119P: Unsharp-masked ring morphology is uncertain due to the technique's arbitrariness
- 2020A&A...644A.119P: Excitation temperature must be assumed since only one line per species
- 2019ApJ...871..170M: Rgd for diffuse Milky Way gas may not apply to the dense CMZ
- 2019ApJ...871..170M: H3O+/SO ratio affected by optical depth and calibration; factor of two differences possible
- 2019ApJ...871..170M: Total Power data unusable so no zero-spacing beyond ACA
- 2014Sci...345.1584B: Preliminary LTE model not fully optimized for ALMA; abundance uncertainties exclude free-free contamination and dust property uncertainties
- 2020ApJ...902..110D: Constant alpha_CO may be invalid at z>3
- 2025A&A...698A.204H: Gas mass has large systematic uncertainties from alpha_CO, which are ignored; CI excitation not constrained
- 2025A&A...698A.204H: Simulation comparison is only qualitative
- 2017AJ....154...11H: Radio noise value is approximate; ALMA compact-configuration uncertainty may be underestimated
- 2019A&A...622A..26G: CF+ and C3H+ lines are weak and contaminated; Galactic center abundances cannot be determined absolutely
- 2025NatAs...9.1476C: HDO and H2O observed ~2 weeks apart; Q(H2O) inferred via CH3OH proxy
- 2025NatAs...9.1476C: Low S/N of HDO leaves L_p unconstrained for 50% distributed case
- 2013ApJ...778L..25C: Emitting region unresolved; higher resolution and 2D/3D modeling needed
- 2019A&A...631A..64B: Some channels not cleaned to threshold in combined 12CO image
- 2019A&A...628A..10B: Line-continuum splitting is preliminary with unexplained baseline artifacts
- 2020ApJ...896...35J: Free-free contribution at 1.2 mm not removed; relative astrometry insufficient
- 2019A&A...623A.124C: Ratio uncertain by a factor of a few; assumes CH3OH shares H2CO emitting area; distance of 122 pc used
- 2026ApJ..1000L..32A: Small sample; single-component fit; OPR fixed at 3
- 2017A&A...598A..53D: Inhomogeneous data not aimed at AlO; low sensitivity; LTE optically thin assumption likely invalid
- 2018ApJ...866L..12G: Deblending of HNC/CN depends strongly on redshift; outflow rate cannot be estimated; limited tracers
- 2024BAAA...65..173M: Preliminary results; further analysis in future work
- 2024IJAsB..23...14M: Hyperfine lines unresolved and source not spatially resolved
- 2020A&A...644A..84M: Tex-Ntot degeneracy for AA gives a factor ~2 uncertainty on Ntot
- 2020A&A...644A..84M: Some MF transitions under-reproduced; unidentified blends possible
- 2014ApJ...781L..39T: Redshift remains ambiguous; further CO transitions needed
- 2014ApJ...781L..39T: Simulation not verified at high z for bright CO emitters
- 2020ApJ...893..101L: Flux ratios are only a rough abundance proxy; high-Eu lines biased by temperature
- 2018ApJ...863..129S: Possible synchrotron contamination of 110 GHz SFR (~25%); absolute values uncertain due to conversion factors
- 2015ApJ...803...97S: Many lines blended; Hot Core v_t=2 T_rot not determinable
- 2021A&A...646A..76L: Field LF based on a single source; large uncertainties
- 2017ApJ...843...27L: Tex is poorly constrained because data points are scattered at low S/N; may be underestimated by factor ~2
- 2017ApJ...843...27L: Disk is optically thick in dust so molecules near the midplane cannot be probed
- 2019ApJ...882..118X: Uncertainties may be underestimated since continuum subtraction systematics not included
- 2020ApJ...889..178B: Largest uncertainty is the poorly constrained mass of Src x
- 2019A&A...623L...6P: Testing desorption mechanisms needs higher resolution and multi-molecule modeling
- 2024ApJ...974...83Y: Inner disk structure is an extrapolation of the outer disk
- 2024ApJ...974...83Y: Flux calibration systematic uncertainty not included
- 2019A&A...623L...1K: CO/OH results are tentative due to simple methods; non-LTE modelling needed
- 2016ApJ...822...80S: Single magnification used for lensing correction is a simplification
- 2016ApJ...822...80S: Not enough high-z size measurements to exclude size evolution
- 2024ApJ...962...48J: Single-temperature, single-velocity assumption and non-LTE excitation of some lines (5-4) not explored
- 2024ApJ...962...48J: Dust temperature not well known and assumed equal to Trot
- 2016ApJ...827...72S: Trot=100 K assumed for most molecules; SO abundance relies on a single 33SO line; H2CS single low S/N line
- 2019A&A...628A..27B: Ages unreliable because the same accretion history is assumed for all sources; no CR attenuation.
- 2020MNRAS.497.5454I: Radio components may be knots of a single jet so member count may be lower
- 2017A&A...606A.125S: N2D+ is weak, on edge of atmospheric feature, continuum subtraction less accurate
- 2017A&A...606A.125S: Isothermal vertical temperature assumption and no vertical abundance distribution
- 2024AJ....167...66Y: Emission only marginally resolved; midplane assumption; CH2DOH spectroscopy uncertain by ~factor 3
- 2018ApJ...855..113D: Only one FeO transition detected; collisional rates unknown; source unresolved
- 2019MNRAS.490.1220K: Lensing magnification bias of background quasars remains a systematic issue
- 2019MNRAS.490.1220K: Conversion N(CO) to N(H2) is uncertain and not constant
- 2018AJ....155...47A: Mass limit depends on opacity and temperature; only particles smaller than wavelength detectable
- 2018AJ....155...47A: ALMA velocity resolution coarse
- 2017MNRAS.469.2230M: H2 column is a lower limit, so abundances are upper limits as dust may be optically thick
- 2017MNRAS.469.2230M: NH2CHO underproduced by model by factor 10
- 2020A&A...635A..48M: Statistical errors not conservative given LTE assumptions; neglected effects such as beam dilution and self-absorption
- 2017A&A...605A..21C: Inner 50 AU cannot be modeled due to low resolution and dust optical depth
- 2017A&A...605A..21C: Matched-filter fluxes are only lower limits
- 2017A&A...605A..21C: Parameterized models include no chemistry; formation route cannot be distinguished
- 2024ApJ...966..119L: Velocity resolution and S/N are too low to robustly examine arm kinematics and spirals
- 2018ApJ...857...35S: Distance is uncertain; resolution too low to resolve internal structure or confirm rotation
- 2018ApJ...853L..19S: Dust emissivity uncertain; coagulation on small scales could lower N(H2) and raise abundances
- 2019ApJ...880..130M: Column densities are lower limits because of maximum source size; extended methanol may be filtered out by lack of short baselines; possible optical thickness
- 2017A&A...604L...2F: Gas-phase formation routes cannot be ruled out
- 2019ApJ...872..196S: Rotation temperatures are upper limits and column densities lower limits because low-Eu lines may be optically thick; large uncertainty in 13CH3OH columns; assumed 200 K
- 2019A&A...624A..70C: Neither data processing nor LTE modeling was optimized to reproduce line intensities
- 2019ApJ...885...82L: H2C34S column density may be underestimated due to narrow linewidth (2 channels)
- 2017A&A...597A..53L: Tex hard to constrain for propanal and acetone; uncertainties dominated by LTE and Gaussian assumptions
- 2017A&A...606L...7B: Higher spatial resolution is needed to distinguish between scenarios; synthetic predictions needed for the disk wind
- 2016A&A...595L...4L: Source size from three low-energy lines; higher-energy lines likely more compact, affecting column density; higher resolution needed

