### 2025A&A...694A.166C: The ALMA-ATOMS survey: Vibrationally excited HC<SUB>3</SUB>N lines in hot cores (2025; star_formation, astrochemistry, milky_way_ism; archival_reuse)
- question: How do the physical conditions in hot cores affect the excitation of vibrationally excited HC3N lines (HC3N*), observed at 3 mm in 60 hot cores?
- step 1: Identify HC3N* lines and fit LTE model
  - method: Spectra at hot-core peak; XCLASS LTE fit with CDMS/JPL line data; free parameters: source size, Trot, N, line width, velocity offset; same abundance for all states [3.1 HC3N* line identification: "by setting the deconvolved size of the continuum core, rotation temperature, source-averaged column density, line width, and velocity offset as free parameters in the fitting process"]
