  - assumption: mu=2.8; kappa=0.24 cm2/g; gas-to-dust ratio from R_GC relation [3.2.2 Parameter calculation: "where $\mu\approx2.8$ is the mean particle weight per $\rm H_2$ molecule"]
- result: Hot cores with HC3N* detected = 52 of 60 ± not stated count [abstract: "We have detected HC$_3$N\* lines in 52 hot cores, 29 of which show more than one vibrationally excited state."]
- result: Rotation temperature range = 160 to 335 K, mean 235 K ± (160±18) to (335±22) K; mean ±21 K [3.2.2 Parameter calculation: "the rotation temperature ranges from (160$\pm$18) to (335$\pm$22) K, with a mean value of (235$\pm$21) K"]
- result: HC3N* column density range = 6.9e15 to 1.7e18 ± ±0.3e15 and ±0.1e18 cm^-2 [3.2.2 Parameter calculation: "ranges from (6.9$\pm$0.3)$\times$10$^{15}$ to (1.7$\pm$0.1)$\times$10$^{18}$ cm$^{-2}$"]
- result: n(H2) of cores with HC3N* = 1.3e5 to 5.0e8, mean 3.2e7 ± ±0.2e5, ±0.5e8 cm^-3 [3.2.2 Parameter calculation: "ranges from (1.3$\pm$0.2)$\times$10${^5}$ to (5.0$\pm$0.5)$\times$10$^{8}$ cm$^{-3}$, with a mean value of 3.2$\times$10$^{7}$ cm$^{-3}$"]
- result: Detection rate of v7=1 = 87% ± not stated percent [3.1 HC3N* line identification: "The detection rates for v$_7$=1, v$_7$=2, v$_6$=1, v$_5$=1, v$_7$=3, v$_6$=v$_7$=1, and v$_4$=1 are 87%, 48%, 45%, 27%, 27%, 25%, and 3%, respectively."]
- result: HC3N* abundance range = 6.9e-10 to 2.3e-7 ± ±1.5e-10, ±0.2e-7 dimensionless [3.2.2 Parameter calculation: "ranges from (6.9$\pm$1.5)$\times$10$^{-10}$ to (2.3$\pm$0.2)$\times$10$^{-7}$"]
- limitation (authors): 3 mm data cannot resolve the emission distribution in distant sources [3.3 Spatial distributions: "since these two sources are located at very large distances, we were unable to resolve the emission distribution with 3 mm data."]
