### 2020ApJ...889..178B: The Orion Protostellar Explosion and Runaway Stars Revisited: Stellar Masses, Disk Retention, and an Outflow from the Becklin-Neugebauer Object (2020; star_formation; multi_facility_alma_minor)
- question: What masses of the runaway stars Src I, BN and Src x follow from center-of-mass momentum constraints, do the radio knots near BN trace an outflow from BN, and did the disks survive the ejection?
- step 1: Center-of-mass constraint on masses
  - method: Compute CoM velocity of BN, Src I, Src x over grids of masses with proper motion errors, requiring CoM speed below OMC1 escape/circular speed [Constraints on Stellar Masses: "We used these measurements and their errors to compute the motion of the center of mass (CoM) on the plane of the sky of the three ejected stars"]
  - parameter: Mx 1-4, MBN 8-18, MI 5-25 Msun [Constraints on Stellar Masses: "the mass of Src I is allowed to vary from $M_I$ = 5 to 25 M$_{\odot}$ in increments of 1 M$_{\odot}$"]
  - assumption: OMC1 at rest in ONC frame; D = 400 pc [Constraints on Stellar Masses: "It is assumed that OMC1 is stationary in the reference frame defined by stars in Orion Nebula Cluster."]
  - validation: Error circles from varying speeds and position angles [Constraints on Stellar Masses: "results in an error circle with a radius of about 0.6 km s$^{-1}$"]
- result: Src I mass = ~15 ± not stated Msun [abstract: "Src I) is likely to have a mass around 15 M$_{\odot}$"]
- result: CoM motion error circle (all varied) = 0.6 ± not stated km/s [Constraints on Stellar Masses: "results in an error circle with a radius of about 0.6 km s$^{-1}$"]
- limitation (authors): Largest uncertainty is the poorly constrained mass of Src x [Constraints on Stellar Masses: "the largest uncertainty is caused by the relatively poorly constrained mass of Src x"]
- not stated (card): ALMA data processing, imaging parameters and CASA version; Details of how the ALMA upper limits were measured; Proper motion fitting method for the VLA knots (deferred to Vargas-Gonzalez et al. in prep.); Registration uncertainties of IR images

